  "caption": "Quinn's first trail run met one tree root, and Quinn landed right on the point of the shoulder. Now there's a little bump on top, which Quinn named Gerald.\n\nA fall onto the shoulder can sprain the AC joint, the small joint on top of the shoulder. It's not the same as a dislocation, and an X-ray may be needed to rule out a broken collarbone.\n\nWhat often helps: a sling for comfort only, ice and gentle movement early, gradually raising the arm, building strength with rows and band work, then easing into pressing. A small bump often stays and is usually cosmetic.\n\nMarked deformity, numbness, severe pain or ongoing pain on top of the shoulder are worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
